210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 132 0 R
/E (The financial literacy program for women in tribal communities focuses on empowering participants through essential skills and knowledge. It covers foundational concepts such as income, expenses, budgeting, and saving techniques, enabling women to manage their finances effectively. Participants also learn about financial products and the importance of financial planning, fostering confidence in their financial decisions. Community support through peer learning and savings groups enhances the overall experience, promoting collaboration and sustainable financial practices within the community.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
